<!--
  The wordmark.

  Letterforms are strokes rather than filled outlines. A launcher icon gives the
  name about nine device-independent pixels of height to live in, and an even
  monoline stays readable there where a contrasted typeface would break up.

  Two constraints shaped the spacing. Everything sits inside the 66dp adaptive
  safe zone, so no launcher mask can clip a letter; and the gap between letter
  boxes is wider than the stroke, because the strokes are centred on those
  edges and a narrower gap makes neighbouring letters touch.

  Doubles as the monochrome layer for themed icons: it is only the name, with
  no background of its own, so the system can tint it whole.
-->
